{"black_box_warning":{"current_value":"Current row boxed-warning text for FINTEPLA valvular heart disease and pulmonary arterial hypertension.","fda_source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212102s016lbl.pdf","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22e88f360e-33ad-4cd6-b2de-5ef885857c5d%22&limit=5"],"proposed_value":"Keep current boxed-warning text; replace the source field with FDA/accessdata or FDA/openFDA metadata, not DailyMed.","rationale":"FDA accessdata labeling contains the same boxed warning and supports VHD/PAH echocardiogram monitoring and FINTEPLA REMS. The current source field cites DailyMed, which is not permissible for boxed-warning verification under the audit policy.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified"},"blocking_questions":[],"fact_checks":[{"current_value":"fenfluramine; trade_names=Fintepla; alternate_generic_names blank; pubmed_search_aliases=ZX008","field":"generic_name / trade_names / alternate_generic_names / pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"alternate_generic_names: fenfluramine hydrochloride; fenfluramine HCl. trade_names: Fintepla; Pondimin (historical/withdrawn anorectic); Ponderex (historical/withdrawn anorectic). Keep pubmed_search_aliases: ZX008.","rationale":"Generic name fenfluramine, Fintepla, and ZX008 are supported. FDA clinical review also identifies historical Pondimin/Ponderex and fenfluramine HCl, so the empty alternate_generic_names field and current trade_names omit important aliases. Dexfenfluramine/Redux is a distinct d-enantiomer, not a fenfluramine alias.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212102s016lbl.pdf","https://www.fda.gov/media/158280/download","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT02682927","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT03355209"]},{"current_value":"available_in_us=Yes; epilepsy_type=Dravet; LGS; formulations_available=Oral solution; filter_availability=Available in US; filter_epilepsy_type=Dravet; LGS; filter_formulation=Liquid","field":"availability_indication_formulation","proposed_value":"No change.","rationale":"FDA labeling supports current U.S. availability, indication for seizures associated with Dravet syndrome and Lennox-Gastaut syndrome in patients 2 years and older, and oral solution 2.2 mg/mL formulation.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212102s016lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"typical_doses_per_day=Dravet/LGS: 0.2-0.7 mg/kg/day divided BID subject to syndrome/background therapy caps; minimum_effective_dose=0.2 mg/kg/day; maximum_approved_daily_dose=0.7 mg/kg/day; capped by product labeling and lower with stiripentol","field":"dose_fields","proposed_value":"Preferred label-aligned wording: Initial dosage 0.1 mg/kg twice daily (0.2 mg/kg/day). Maximum without concomitant stiripentol plus clobazam: 0.35 mg/kg twice daily (0.7 mg/kg/day; max 26 mg/day). Maximum with concomitant stiripentol plus clobazam: 0.2 mg/kg twice daily (0.4 mg/kg/day; max 17 mg/day). Additional caps apply with strong CYP1A2/CYP2D6 inhibitors, severe renal impairment, or hepatic impairment.","rationale":"The current dose fields are broadly correct but omit the explicit 26 mg/day and 17 mg/day caps and the twice-daily label wording.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212102s016lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"half_life_range=~20 h; major_organ_for_metabolism=Liver; enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting=Not a major enzyme inducer/inhibitor; CYP2D6/1A2/2B6 metabolism; filter_enzyme_effect=Inducer; Inhibitor","field":"metabolism_enzyme_fields","proposed_value":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting: Not a major enzyme inducer/inhibitor; primarily metabolized by CYP1A2, CYP2B6, and CYP2D6. filter_enzyme_effect: Neither inducer nor inhibitor.","rationale":"FDA labeling supports 20-hour half-life, metabolism primarily by CYP1A2/CYP2B6/CYP2D6, and no clinically relevant CYP induction or inhibition by fenfluramine/norfenfluramine. The filter_enzyme_effect value contradicts this.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212102s016lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"mechanism_of_action includes unknown seizure mechanism, serotonin 5-HT2 agonist activity, and proposed sigma-1 modulation; mechanism_source=FDA/DailyMed labeling; American Epilepsy Society 2024 U.S. ASM summary; mechanism_source_tier=FDA label; filter_mechanism=Serotonin / sigma","field":"mechanism_fields","proposed_value":"If using FDA-only support: Precise seizure mechanism is unknown; fenfluramine and norfenfluramine exhibit agonist activity at serotonin 5-HT2 receptors. If retaining sigma-1 modulation, add a trusted PubMed/NCBI peer-reviewed mechanism source and change mechanism_source_tier away from FDA-only.","rationale":"FDA labeling supports unknown mechanism and serotonin 5-HT2 receptor agonist activity, but not sigma-1 modulation. DailyMed and AES are not acceptable trusted source entries for this audit bundle as written.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"missing_source","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212102s016lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"qt_interval_effect=No clinically meaningful QT prolongation in labeling; cardiac valvulopathy/pulmonary hypertension monitoring required; filter_qt_effect=No known meaningful QT effect; QT prolongation","field":"qt_fields","proposed_value":"qt_interval_effect: No clinically meaningful QT prolongation in labeling; cardiac valvulopathy/pulmonary hypertension monitoring required. filter_qt_effect: No known meaningful QT effect.","rationale":"FDA labeling states FINTEPLA did not prolong QT at 4 times the maximum recommended dose. The filter value should not include QT prolongation.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212102s016lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"GI: decreased appetite 38%, constitutional: fatigue/lethargy 16%, GI: diarrhea 15%, CNS: somnolence 13%, cardiac: valvular heart disease 0% in controlled trials","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"At labeled 0.7 mg/kg/day arms: decreased appetite 38% (DS) / 36% (LGS); somnolence/sedation/lethargy 25% (DS) / 22% (LGS); diarrhea 15% (DS) / 13% (LGS); fatigue/malaise/asthenia 10% (DS) / 24% (LGS). No VHD/PAH occurred in DS/LGS clinical trials up to 3 years, but postmarketing VHD/PAH cases have been reported.","rationale":"FDA adverse-reaction tables do not support fatigue/lethargy 16% or somnolence 13% for the maximum labeled dose arms. VHD/PAH absence in controlled/extension trial monitoring is supported, with postmarketing cases noted in labeling.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212102s016lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"year_fda_cleared=2020 for Dravet; 2022 LGS; older anorectic approval withdrawn; status_or_notes=current ASM for DS/LGS and historical anorectic withdrawal","field":"approval_history_status","proposed_value":"2020 for Dravet; 2022 for LGS; original anorectic approval in 1973 as Pondimin/Ponderex, withdrawn from the U.S. market in 1997 for safety reasons.","rationale":"FDA approval letter and orphan-drug listing support June 25, 2020 Dravet approval. FDA 2022 supplement approval letter supports LGS. FDA clinical review supports 1973 anorectic history and 1997 withdrawal.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/appletter/2020/212102Orig1s000ltr.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/appletter/2022/212102Orig1s003ltr.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/opdlisting/oopd/detailedIndex.cfm?cfgridkey=414613","https://www.fda.gov/media/158280/download"]},{"current_value":"evidence_sources=Epilepsy Society ASM list; FDA/DailyMed labeling; American Epilepsy Society 2024 U.S. ASM summary","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata prescribing information; FDA/openFDA drug label API; FDA approval letters and clinical review; ClinicalTrials.gov; PubMed RCT records","rationale":"The named Epilepsy Society and AES sources are not in the trusted-source domain list provided for this audit, and DailyMed is not permissible for boxed-warning verification.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212102s016lbl.pdf","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22e88f360e-33ad-4cd6-b2de-5ef885857c5d%22&limit=5","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT02682927","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT02926898","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT03355209"]}],"generic_name":"fenfluramine","missing_rcts":[],"outcome_checks":[{"current_value":"15-66.6 % with Sullivan2023 66.6%; Knupp2022 15%; Nabbout2020 49%","field":"diff_50_responder_maximum_effective_dose / plot_diff_50_responder_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"No numeric change for currently cited plot values. Consider adding Lagae2019 RR50 only if full-text or FDA-label responder-category extraction is accepted for this dataset.","rationale":"Sullivan2023 reports 72.9% versus 6.3% RR50 at 0.7 mg/kg/day, differential 66.6. Knupp2022 reports 25% versus 10%, differential 15. Nabbout2020 reports 54% versus 5%, differential 49. The current plot entries match those cited values.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37543865/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35499850/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31790543/","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT02682927","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT02926898","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT03355209"]},{"current_value":"19.9-64.8 % described as drug-minus-placebo MPC differential for Sullivan2023, Knupp2022, Nabbout2020, Lagae2019","field":"diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose / plot_diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"19.9-64.8 % (reported placebo-adjusted or drug-minus-placebo seizure-frequency change at maximum effective dose/regimen: Sullivan2023 fenfluramine 0.7 mg/kg/day placebo-adjusted greater reduction in MCSF 64.8%; Knupp2022 fenfluramine 0.7 mg/kg/day estimated median difference vs placebo 19.9 percentage points; Nabbout2020 fenfluramine 0.4 mg/kg/day with stiripentol placebo-adjusted greater reduction in MCSF 54.0%; Lagae2019 fenfluramine 0.7 mg/kg/day median reduction 74.9% vs placebo 19.2%, arithmetic differential 55.7%).","rationale":"The numeric values are supported by the cited RCT/outcome evidence, but the current wording overstates them as uniform drug-minus-placebo median percent-change differentials. Sullivan2023 and Nabbout2020 are placebo-adjusted/model-based greater reductions; Knupp2022 is an estimated median difference; Lagae2019 is the arithmetic median reduction difference.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37543865/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35499850/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31790543/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31862249/","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212102s016lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo seizure-freedom patient-rate differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen","field":"diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose / plot_diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"-1 to 8 percentage points among extractable maximum-dose/regimen RCT sources: Lagae2019/Study 1 fenfluramine 0.7 mg/kg/day 8% vs 0% placebo, diff 8%; Nabbout2020/Study 2 fenfluramine 0.4 mg/kg/day with stiripentol 2% vs 0% placebo, diff 2%; Knupp2022/LGS fenfluramine 0.7 mg/kg/day 0% vs 1% placebo, diff -1 percentage point. Sullivan2023 complete seizure-freedom differential was not verified from a trusted accessible abstract in this audit.","rationale":"FDA labeling explicitly reports no-convulsive-seizure patient rates for the Dravet Study 1/2 maximum regimens, and Knupp2022 reports LGS seizure freedom by group. Therefore the blanket NR/not extractable value is not correct for all included RCT evidence.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212102s016lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35499850/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31790543/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31862249/"]}],"overall_status":"needs_update","proposed_row_updates":[{"current_value":"","field":"alternate_generic_names","proposed_value":"fenfluramine hydrochloride; fenfluramine HCl","reason":"Important salt/alias names are used in FDA and trial records.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212102s016lbl.pdf","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT02682927"]},{"current_value":"Fintepla","field":"trade_names","proposed_value":"Fintepla; Pondimin (historical/withdrawn anorectic); Ponderex (historical/withdrawn anorectic)","reason":"FDA clinical review identifies historical fenfluramine trade names; adding them reduces duplicate-row risk.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.fda.gov/media/158280/download"]},{"current_value":"Inducer; Inhibitor","field":"filter_enzyme_effect","proposed_value":"Neither inducer nor inhibitor","reason":"FDA label states fenfluramine/norfenfluramine are not CYP inhibitors or inducers at clinically relevant concentrations.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212102s016lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"No known meaningful QT effect; QT prolongation","field":"filter_qt_effect","proposed_value":"No known meaningful QT effect","reason":"FDA label states FINTEPLA did not prolong QT at 4 times the maximum recommended dose.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212102s016lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"GI: decreased appetite 38%, constitutional: fatigue/lethargy 16%, GI: diarrhea 15%, CNS: somnolence 13%, cardiac: valvular heart disease 0% in controlled trials","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"At labeled 0.7 mg/kg/day arms: decreased appetite 38% (DS) / 36% (LGS); somnolence/sedation/lethargy 25% (DS) / 22% (LGS); diarrhea 15% (DS) / 13% (LGS); fatigue/malaise/asthenia 10% (DS) / 24% (LGS). No VHD/PAH occurred in DS/LGS clinical trials up to 3 years, but postmarketing VHD/PAH cases have been reported.","reason":"Current adverse-event percentages mix unsupported values with supported maximum-dose values.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212102s016lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"19.9-64.8 % (drug minus placebo MPC differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Sullivan2023 fenfluramine 0.7 mg/kg/day 64.8%; Knupp2022 fenfluramine 0.7 mg/kg/day 19.9%; Nabbout2020 fenfluramine 0.4 mg/kg/day with stiripentol 54%; Lagae2019 fenfluramine 0.7 mg/kg/day 55.7%)","field":"diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"19.9-64.8 % (reported placebo-adjusted or drug-minus-placebo seizure-frequency change at maximum effective dose/regimen: Sullivan2023 fenfluramine 0.7 mg/kg/day placebo-adjusted greater reduction in MCSF 64.8%; Knupp2022 fenfluramine 0.7 mg/kg/day estimated median difference vs placebo 19.9 percentage points; Nabbout2020 fenfluramine 0.4 mg/kg/day with stiripentol placebo-adjusted greater reduction in MCSF 54.0%; Lagae2019 fenfluramine 0.7 mg/kg/day median reduction 74.9% vs placebo 19.2%, arithmetic differential 55.7%).","reason":"Numbers are supported, but current wording incorrectly treats all as the same median percent-change differential type.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37543865/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35499850/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31790543/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31862249/"]},{"current_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo seizure-freedom patient-rate differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","field":"diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"-1 to 8 percentage points among extractable maximum-dose/regimen RCT sources: Lagae2019/Study 1 fenfluramine 0.7 mg/kg/day 8% vs 0% placebo, diff 8%; Nabbout2020/Study 2 fenfluramine 0.4 mg/kg/day with stiripentol 2% vs 0% placebo, diff 2%; Knupp2022/LGS fenfluramine 0.7 mg/kg/day 0% vs 1% placebo, diff -1 percentage point. Sullivan2023 complete seizure-freedom differential not verified from a trusted accessible abstract in this audit.","reason":"Seizure-freedom/no-convulsive-seizure values are extractable for several maximum-dose/regimen RCTs.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212102s016lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35499850/"]},{"current_value":"","field":"plot_diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"Lagae2019|8|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31862249/|119; Nabbout2020|2|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31790543/|87; Knupp2022|-1|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35499850/|263","reason":"Plot field is empty despite extractable study-level seizure-freedom/no-convulsive-seizure differentials.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212102s016lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35499850/"]},{"current_value":"Sullivan2023|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37543865/; Knupp2022|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35499850/; Sullivan2021|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33540241/; Nabbout2020|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31790543/; Lagae2019|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31862249/","field":"pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links","proposed_value":"Sullivan2023|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37543865/; Knupp2022|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35499850/; Nabbout2020|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31790543/; Lagae2019|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31862249/","reason":"Sullivan2021 is a responder/NNT secondary analysis of trial data, not a primary phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT report. Reclassify rather than treat as a primary RCT link.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33540241/","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT02682927","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT02926898"]},{"current_value":"PubMed loop 22/65 on 2026-05-15: 5 qualifying placebo-controlled randomized clinical trial report(s) retained from 13 PubMed candidate(s). Links were rebuilt from fetched PubMed PMID metadata and named FirstAuthorYear. Differential effectiveness columns summarize extractable maximum effective dose/regimen values within qualifying RCT reports.","field":"rct_pubmed_verification_notes","proposed_value":"Audit 2026-05-21: 4 primary phase II/III placebo-controlled randomized trial reports retained (Sullivan2023, Knupp2022, Nabbout2020, Lagae2019). Sullivan2021 is a responder/NNT secondary analysis of phase 3 trial data and should be reclassified if this field is reserved for primary RCT reports. Differential effectiveness columns summarize extractable maximum effective dose/regimen values from cited RCT/outcome sources.","reason":"Current note counts Sullivan2021 as a qualifying primary RCT report.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33540241/"]}],"rct_link_checks":[{"label":"Sullivan2023","pmid":"37543865","proposed_action":"Retain.","rationale":"Fenfluramine in Dravet syndrome; multicenter randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, parallel-group phase 3 trial; 143 randomized; supports Sullivan2023 RR50 and 64.8% placebo-adjusted MCSF reduction values.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37543865/"},{"label":"Knupp2022","pmid":"35499850","proposed_action":"Retain.","rationale":"Fenfluramine in Lennox-Gastaut syndrome; randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase 3 trial; ClinicalTrials.gov NCT03355209; supports LGS RR50 and median-difference outcome values.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35499850/"},{"label":"Sullivan2021","pmid":"33540241","proposed_action":"Reclassify as secondary responder/NNT analysis; remove from pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links if that field is reserved for primary RCT reports.","rationale":"The article analyzes responder thresholds and NNT from existing fenfluramine RCT data. It is useful secondary evidence but is not itself a primary placebo-controlled phase II/III RCT report.","status":"not_placebo_rct","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33540241/"},{"label":"Nabbout2020","pmid":"31790543","proposed_action":"Retain.","rationale":"Fenfluramine in Dravet syndrome receiving stiripentol-inclusive regimens; randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase 3 trial; ClinicalTrials.gov NCT02926898; supports 54% placebo-adjusted MCSF reduction and RR50 54% vs 5%.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31790543/"},{"label":"Lagae2019","pmid":"31862249","proposed_action":"Retain.","rationale":"Fenfluramine hydrochloride in Dravet syndrome; randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase 3 trial; FDA label Study 1 corresponds to the pivotal no-stiripentol DS trial and supports the cited median-reduction outcome.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31862249/"}],"source_updates":[{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=boxed_warning_found; setid=e88f360e-33ad-4cd6-b2de-5ef885857c5d; published=Nov 17, 2025; title=FINTEPLA (FENFLURAMINE) SOLUTION [UCB, INC.]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=e88f360e-33ad-4cd6-b2de-5ef885857c5d","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata prescribing information; status=boxed_warning_found; NDA=212102; label=212102s016; revised=04/2025; title=FINTEPLA (fenfluramine) oral solution; url=https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212102s016lbl.pdf; FDA/openFDA API url=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22e88f360e-33ad-4cd6-b2de-5ef885857c5d%22&limit=5","reason":"DailyMed is not permissible for black-box warning verification; FDA/accessdata and openFDA are permissible.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212102s016lbl.pdf","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22e88f360e-33ad-4cd6-b2de-5ef885857c5d%22&limit=5"]},{"current_value":"05-20-2026","field":"fda_black_box_warning_verified","proposed_value":"05-21-2026","reason":"FDA source was rechecked during this audit on the current system date.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212102s016lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Epilepsy Society ASM list; FDA/DailyMed labeling; American Epilepsy Society 2024 U.S. ASM summary","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata prescribing information; FDA/openFDA drug label API; FDA approval letters and clinical review; ClinicalTrials.gov; PubMed RCT records","reason":"Use only trusted domains and avoid DailyMed for boxed warning.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212102s016lbl.pdf","https://www.fda.gov/media/158280/download","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT02682927","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT02926898","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT03355209"]}],"summary":"Fenfluramine row is mostly supported for U.S. availability, DS/LGS indication, oral solution formulation, dosing framework, metabolism, half-life, QT statement, FDA boxed warning text, and four primary placebo-controlled RCT links. Updates are needed for the boxed-warning source, missing aliases/historical trade names, incorrect filter flags for enzyme and QT effects, adverse-event percentages, over-specific median-percent-change wording, seizure-freedom extraction, and reclassification of Sullivan2021 as a secondary responder/NNT analysis rather than a primary RCT report."}
